==Trivia==
*[[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]], [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dom Cat]], Ninja Cat and [[Zombie Cat (Special Cat)|Zombie Cat]] all had their Strong Against ability removed in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] and readded in [[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.7 Update|Version 2.0.7]].
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Frog Ninja Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Shonen Manga (Removed Combo)|Shonen Manga]].
*Ninja Cat is one of the many units who were updated to have multi-hit in [[Version 6.0 Update|Version 6.0]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.5 Update|Version 15.5]], Ninja Cat and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] became unlockable after clearing the [[Philippines (Empire of Cats)|Philippines/Ōita Prefecture]], rather than [[Cambodia (Empire of Cats)|Cambodia/Miyazaki Prefecture]].
*Her position is higher form by form.
*Frog Ninja Cat might be a reference to the Japanese book ''[[wikipedia:Jiraiya#Classic tale|The Tale of the Gallant Jiraiya]]'', where a man saves a giant toad from an even bigger snake. The toad then teaches him toad magic, with one of the spells letting the man summon a toad to aid him in battle.
*Flying Ninja Cat's movement animation is identical to Kanzo Hattori's "Flying Squirrel Technique" in ''[[wikipedia:Ninja Hattori-kun|Ninja Hattori-kun]]'', and her parachute looks just like Hattori's outside of having a swirl-pattern design. Furthermore, her Japanese name is Flying Squirrel Ninja Cat.
**Incidentally, Hattori is afraid of frogs, which may be why Frog Ninja Cat only rides another Ninja Cat in a frog mask.
**The parachute also somewhat resembles the pattern on the inside of the [[Cat Base Menu|Cat Base]].
*Her gender is confirmed by the Caltrops' description in [[The Burgle Cats]]: "Ninja Cat forgot to clean up after herself. Just rubber, but the pointy bits still hurt when stepped on! Imagine if it was actual steel!"
*In The Battle Cats Unite!, her True Form is still playable, however, it is only accessible via save file editing.
*Prior to [[Version 15.6 Update|Version 15.6]], Ninja Cat's Evolved Form was named Ninja Frog Cat, and her descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Ninja Cat
One of the strongest fighters.
Rivals with Axe Cat. 10 wins, 1 loss.
Strong against Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Ninja Frog Cat
Learned how to summon animals.
Rides a frog for better mobility.
Strong against Red enemies.</pre>
<pre>Flying Ninja Cat
Dances across the sky, assaulting enemies
using advanced ninjutsu. Cheap to produce,
very strong against Red enemies!</pre>

